Status:
- `1B` gap: partly resolved
- `2B` gap: partly resolved
- `3B` gap: partly resolved
- `4B` gap: partly resolved
- `7B` gap: not recoverable on direct personal-benefit/recusal proof from the current record
- `8B` gap: partly resolved

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Intel to build $20B Ohio chip facility amid global shortage","publisher":"The Associated Press","publication_date":"2022-01-21","url":"https://www.ap.org/news-highlights/spotlights/2022/intel-to-build-20b-ohio-chip-facility-amid-global-shortage/","claim":"Intel announced a $20 billion Ohio chip facility expected to create 3,000 company jobs and 7,000 construction jobs, and Biden used the announcement to push CHIPS funding.","locator":"lines 91-100, 113-121","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous AP reporting with direct event details and attributed quotes.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 announcement tied to the semiconductor policy push.","ruler_attribution":"Partial: the investment was private-sector, but Biden publicly used it to advance the CHIPS agenda.","contrary_evidence":["Intel's move also reflected its own supply-chain and business incentives."],"lenses":["8B.1","8B.3","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Biden-Harris Administration Announces CHIPS for America Leadership","publisher":"U.S. Department of Commerce","publication_date":"2022-09-20","url":"https://www.commerce.gov/news/press-releases/2022/09/biden-harris-administration-announces-chips-america-leadership","claim":"Commerce announced CHIPS for America leadership housed at the White House and Commerce, with officials responsible for implementation and interagency coordination.","locator":"lines 305-309","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary official release describing named implementation roles and coordination structure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation step after CHIPS enactment.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal implementation architecture under Biden, though delivery still depended on subordinate agencies.","contrary_evidence":["This is implementation architecture, not proof of delivered outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.3","8B.4","8B.5","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Frequently Asked Questions: CHIPS Act of 2022 Provisions and Implementation","publisher":"Congress.gov | Library of Congress","publication_date":"2023-04-25","url":"https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/R47523","claim":"The first CHIPS NOFO opened the application portal on February 28, 2023, set application steps and deadlines, and required workforce and community investments including sectoral partnerships and prevailing wages.","locator":"lines 926-927, 991-993","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"CRS summary with statutory and program details, useful for tracing the law into implementation rules.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Post-2022 implementation of the 2022 CHIPS law.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal design under Biden's administration, but downstream awards also reflect congressional mandates.","contrary_evidence":["The FAQ summarizes implementation design and eligibility, not completed project delivery."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Biden Invokes Defense Production Act to Accelerate Domestic Manufacturing of Clean Energy","publisher":"U.S. Department of Energy","publication_date":"2022-06-06","url":"https://www.energy.gov/articles/president-biden-invokes-defense-production-act-accelerate-domestic-manufacturing-clean","claim":"Biden issued DPA determinations authorizing DOE to accelerate domestic production of five clean-energy technologies and framed the action as lowering energy costs and supporting good jobs.","locator":"lines 167-180","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary agency announcement of a presidential action and its implementation scope.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct June 2022 executive action.","ruler_attribution":"Strong: the presidential determinations are direct executive action, though funded implementation still depended on Congress and firms.","contrary_evidence":["Subsequent buildout depended on funding, firms, and market conditions."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Announces Guidance on Inflation Reduction Act's Strong Labor Protections","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-11-29","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy1128","claim":"Treasury said initial IRA labor guidance was an important first step to ensure clean-energy tax incentives support good-paying jobs and workforce training.","locator":"lines 605-609","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary implementation guidance with direct description of the rule's purpose.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation of the IRA.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal rule-setting under Biden, though the results depend on compliance and project uptake.","contrary_evidence":["Guidance starts the compliance clock; it does not itself prove realized jobs."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.4","8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Inflation Reduction Act of 2022","publisher":"Internal Revenue Service","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.irs.gov/inflation-reduction-act-of-2022","claim":"IRS said the IRA changed tax laws, provided funds to improve IRS services and technology, and that implementation would not happen immediately because it was a 10-year plan.","locator":"lines 302-307","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official implementation page, but it is general and not a completed-outcome report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Ongoing implementation of the 2022 law.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal administration posture, but not a delivery metric by itself.","contrary_evidence":["No specific completed output is quantified on this page."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Remarks on the Federal Student Loan Debt Relief Program and an Exchange With Reporters","publisher":"The American Presidency Project","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/remarks-the-federal-student-loan-debt-relief-program-and-exchange-with-reporters","claim":"Biden officially launched the student-debt relief application site and said the beta launch handled more than 8 million applications without glitches.","locator":"lines 65-70, 90-92, 112-113","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Archived presidential remarks with direct statements about rollout and use.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 launch of the debt-relief application process.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Biden's announced program and rollout.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is self-report and later court action limited implementation."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Student Loans: Education Should Proactively Manage Fraud Risks in Any Future Debt Relief Efforts","publisher":"U.S. Government Accountability Office","publication_date":"2023-11-16","url":"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-24-107142","claim":"GAO found Education approved an estimated 12 million-plus borrower applicants without evaluating the accuracy and outcomes of its application process and did not apply key fraud-detection processes.","locator":"lines 277-281","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent audit of the 2022 debt-relief rollout and its controls.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Post-2022 review of the 2022 student-debt relief program.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal program design under Biden, but the court stoppage means this measures process quality more than delivered relief.","contrary_evidence":["The program was halted before debt was discharged, so the report does not measure realized relief."],"lenses":["8B.6","8B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bipartisan Infrastructure Law RAISE Grants 2022: Funding Projects in All 50 States","publisher":"U.S. Department of Transportation","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://www.transportation.gov/briefing-room/bipartisan-infrastructure-law-raise-grants-2022-funding-projects-all-50-states","claim":"DOT announced more than $2.2 billion in RAISE funding for 166 projects in urban and rural communities to modernize roads, bridges, transit, rail, ports, and intermodal transportation.","locator":"lines 140-144","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary 2022 grant announcement with direct funding and project counts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation of the infrastructure law.","ruler_attribution":"Strong federal grant execution, though completed projects and outcomes still depend on recipients.","contrary_evidence":["Announced awards are not the same as completed projects or measured outcomes."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.6","8B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Discretionary Grants: DOT Should Improve Clarity and Transparency of Program Management","publisher":"U.S. Government Accountability Office","publication_date":"2024-04-18","url":"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-24-107264","claim":"GAO reported that in fiscal year 2022 DOT awarded about $3.75 billion through the RAISE and INFRA programs and found documentation and transparency weaknesses in grant evaluation.","locator":"lines 275-300","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent oversight report with quantified award totals and process findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Oversight of 2022 IIJA execution, published in 2024.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal administration, with some program management criticism that tempers the claim.","contrary_evidence":["GAO said DOT did not consistently provide complete and accurate documentation and did not fully align evaluation processes with regulations."],"lenses":["8B.2","8B.5","8B.6","8B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Infrastructure Investment and Jobs Act: DOT Should Better Communicate Funding Status and Assess Risks","publisher":"U.S. Government Accountability Office","publication_date":"2025-07-24","url":"https://www.gao.gov/products/gao-25-107166","claim":"GAO found that, as of April 2025, DOT had obligated 59 percent of its available IIJA funding and outlaid over half of that funding to recipients and awardees.","locator":"lines 281-285","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent post-period funding-status review using DOT data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Later trajectory check on the 2022 law's implementation.","ruler_attribution":"Strong for federal implementation trajectory, though this is a later snapshot and not a 2022-only outcome measure.","contrary_evidence":["This is a late snapshot and not a direct 2022 outcome measure."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"The Inflation Reduction Act Is Building a Clean Energy Economy and Good-Paying Jobs","publisher":"Center for American Progress","publication_date":"2023-04-27","url":"https://www.americanprogress.org/article/the-inflation-reduction-act-is-building-a-clean-energy-economy-and-good-paying-jobs/","claim":"CAP testified that the IRA had already created more than 142,000 clean energy jobs and that companies had announced $242 billion in new clean-power capital investments in 41 states.","locator":"lines 238-251","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent policy testimony using outside documentation, but still an advocacy source rather than audited government data.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Early post-enactment outcome evidence for the 2022 IRA.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the law under Biden is the causal frame, but the figures also reflect market response and external documentation.","contrary_evidence":["The figures are compiled and advocacy-oriented rather than a government audit."],"lenses":["8B.7","8B.10","8B.6"]}
